date-released: "2026-05-22"
version: "1.0.2"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility package for the first pre-registered phenome-wide
  Mendelian randomization study of amyloid-PET cortical deposition against
  1,574 FinnGen R12 disease endpoints (N=500,348). The conservative
  wide-APOE-excluded instrument panel localises the AD causal signal to
  the chr1q32.2 CR1 region; the colocalisation replicates cleanly across
  cohort configurations (coloc.abf PP.H4 = 0.983 multi-ethnic primary,
  0.977 NHW EUR-only sub-meta), and per-gene SuSiE fine-mapping on
  full-pairs Brain_Cortex eQTL data (fetched byte-range from the EBI eQTL
  Catalogue) identifies CR1 as the most plausible mediating transcript
  over CR1L (no Brain_Cortex eQTL) and CD46 (credible set 238 kb from
  the amyloid signal). A pre-registered negative-control diagnostic is
  engaged as a tissue-of-action divergence. The deposit includes the
  locked 41-section pre-registration with 4 publicly-versioned amendments,
  the analytical pipeline (R + Python + bash; 18 R scripts including the
  R/17 per-gene SuSiE decomposition, R/19 formal coloc.susie attempt
  with kriging diagnostic, and R/19b cross-cohort coloc.abf cross-check),
  the per-panel instrument lists, the Amyloid-PET Causal Atlas (7,870
  rows × 46 cols) as parquet + TSV + interactive HTML browser, per-stage
  MR result parquets, manuscript figures (including the chr1q32.2
  regional plot), and supplementary tables S1 (per-panel SNP inventory)
  and S2 (per-gene SuSiE credible-set membership). Code is licensed MIT;
  derived data products are licensed CC-BY 4.0 — see LICENSE file for
  full dual-licence terms. Upstream summary-level GWAS data and reference
  panels are not redistributed; canonical sources and SHA256 hashes are
  documented for re-download.
